    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll analyze the existing code structure first to understand how the bulk-approve action is implemented, then implement the new bulk-reject action following the same patterns.\n\nNow I understand the structure. Let me also check the app package to understand the Identity type:\n\nNow I have all the information needed. Let me implement the bulk-reject action following the same patterns as bulk-approve:\n\n1. The schema already supports 'rejected' status and 'bulk-reject.v4' operation\n2. I need to add the bulk-reject handler in approval.go\n3. Register the route in protocol.Routes\n\nNow let me verify the file looks correct:\n\nNow let me build and test to verify the implementation:\n\nBuild succeeded. Let me run the tests:\n\nAll tests pass. The implementation is complete. Let me summarize the changes:\n\n**Changes made to `/Users/administrator/poc-v4b-lanes/qwen3-coder-next/kits/go-manual--005/candidate/internal/candidate/approval.go`:**\n\n1. Added new constant `opReject = \"bulk-reject.v4\"` for the rejection operation\n2. Updated `fingerprint()` to accept operation name parameter (used for both approve and reject)\n3. Added `reject` handler function that:\n   - Validates IDs (no null bytes)\n   - Starts transaction and sets app context (tenant, user, role)\n   - Uses advisory lock with operation+tenant+user+key\n   - Checks for idempotent replay by querying ActionRequest\n   - Queries eligible purchases (tenant matches, created by others, status='submitted')\n   - Returns 409 if any target is ineligible (indistinguishable from missing)\n   - Updates status to 'rejected'\n   - Inserts ApprovalAudit rows with operation='bulk-reject.v4' and toStatus='rejected'\n   - Inserts ActionRequest with operation='bulk-reject.v4' and response JSON\n   - Returns `{\"rejectedIds\":[...]}` with IDs sorted by UTF-8 (already sorted from query)\n4. Registered `/purchases/bulk-reject` route in protocol.Routes\n\nThe implementation follows the exact same patterns as bulk-approve, ensuring:\n- Same validation (Idempotency-Key format, body format, max 100 IDs)\n- Same concurrency control (advisory locks)\n- Same idempotency semantics (replay detection, 409 for mismatched key)\n- Same RLS enforcement through app context\n- Same database transaction atomicity (all or nothing)"
